Rule 17 (If out is provided, and A is 2D, then out must be a scalar of compatible type. Otherwise, out must have the same shape as A, except the last two dimensions.)
{A: tensor, out: tensor} |= if ndim(A) = 2 then (ndim(out) = 0 ∧ ((dtype_(A) = 7 ∧ (dtype_(out) = 7 ∨ dtype_(out) = 8)) ∨ (dtype_(A) = 8 ∧ dtype_(out) = 8) ∨ (dtype_(A) = 9 ∧ (dtype_(out) = 9 ∨ dtype_(out) = 10)) ∨ (dtype_(A) = 10 ∧ dtype_(out) = 10))) else ((∀i ∈ [0, ndim(A) - 2] : shape(A, i) = shape(out, i)) ∧ ((dtype_(A) = 7 ∧ (dtype_(out) = 7 ∨ dtype_(out) = 8)) ∨ (dtype_(A) = 8 ∧ dtype_(out) = 8) ∨ (dtype_(A) = 9 ∧ (dtype_(out) = 9 ∨ dtype_(out) = 10)) ∨ (dtype_(A) = 10 ∧ dtype_(out) = 10)))
>>
Rule 18 (Shape of A must be (*, n, n) where n > 0 and A has at least 2 dimensions)
{A : tensor} |= ndim(A) ≥ 2 ∧ shape(A, ndim(A) - 1) = shape(A, ndim(A) - 2) ∧ shape(A, ndim(A) - 1) > 0
